WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.480
This programme contains
strong language.

2
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.640
So. what made you decide
to leave and come to Moscow?

3
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.416
Because I'm fed up with lying
to the public

4
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.256
about what's really going
on at GCHQ. where I work.

5
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.536
I've done 50 years of service
and I've had enough.

6
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.080
It's time for me to stand up
and say my piece.

7
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.136
50 years of services

8
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.336
and I've had enough.

9
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.376
It's time for me to stand up
and say my piece.

10
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.976
And what is that?

11
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.296
You were friends. weren't you?

12
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.216
That we're no different to what
we're always accusing you lot of.

13
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.336
Hi. Sorry?

14
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.640
You were friends.

15
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.600
Yeah. At least I thought so.

16
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.256
So. what are you looking for?

17
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.456
I don't know.

18
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.336
A clue. Anything.

19
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.536
I just can't believe he'd do this to us.

20
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.560
Us?

21
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.856
He goes missing at the same time

22
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.016
as the biggest leak in intelligence history.

23
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.336
He turns up in Moscow

24
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.456
and admits it on Russian television.

25
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.656
I'd have thought that was
enough evidence...

26
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.720
even for you.

27
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.096
You mean I should get back to work?

28
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.856
That's OK. Saara.

29
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.616
I think we all gave up hope a while back

30
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.640
of you ever actually
doing any work around here.

31
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.240
Can I take this chair?

32
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.760
Don't people hate
having their grammar corrected?

33
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.496
I mean. doesn't it just make
everyone hate you?

34
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.216
If we wrote code as sloppily
as we write English.

35
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.280
it would never run.
Some things have to be right.

36
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.440
Is that all you're having?

37
00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.856
I'm Muslim.

38
00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.559
They don't have anything halal here.

39
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.096
They won't be very welcoming.

40
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.256
What's funny?

41
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.696
No different to any other
department here. then?

42
00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.096
Different FROM any other department.

43
00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.360
It's "different from". "compared with".

44
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.456
No different FROM any other
department.

45
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.000
It's "different from". "compared with".

46
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.680
Different from. compared with.

47
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.160
Different from. compared with.

48
00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:44.240
Different from. compared with.

49
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.576
Because I'm fed up with lying to

50
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.656
the public about what's really
going on at GCHQ. where I work.

51
00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.240
I've done...

52
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.736
stand up and say my piece.

53
00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.216
And what is that?

54
00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.896
That we are no different to what
we're always accusing you...

55
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.096
Yes! What is it?

56
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.296
He said "different to".
He would never say "different to".

57
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.440
He would never make that mistake.
It can't be him.

58
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.640
What? S-Saara. wait.

59
00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.256
Where is he?

60
00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.600
Danny's on his way to London. Saara.

61
00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:43.920
Shit.

62
00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.640
Kathy?

63
00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.656
She's not here.

64
00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.720
Where is she?

65
00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.216
She's gone. What do you mean. "gone"?

66
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.360
What did you say to her?

67
00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.856
I didn't say anything.
I came back and she was packing.

68
00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.760
She's been recalled to Maryland.

69
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.080
She flew about 25 minutes ago.
She left this.

70
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.840
What's going on. Saara?

71
00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.640
Don't lie to me this time.

72
00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.680
You're in love with her. aren't you?

73
00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.400
Don't lie. please.

74
00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.120
I don't know.

75
00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.040
M-Maybe.

76
00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.960
Have you made love here?

77
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.200
Yes.

78
00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.216
OK.

79
00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.400
Where does that leave us?

80
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.440
Do you still love me?

81
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.760
Did you ever really... love me?

82
00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.120
Don't go. James. please. I'm sorry.

83
00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.120
I...

84
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.336
I know you just lost your dad
and I know you're upset.

85
00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:14.016
and I know you say you can't
deal with your emotions.

86
00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.760
I've tried to make allowances.

87
00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.560
I really have.

88
00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.560
But when you crash into
people's lives. people get hurt.

89
00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.200
People who care about you.
People who love you.

90
00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.520
Just try and think about that?

91
00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.280
Fuck.

92
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.000
Mark. welcome.

93
00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:16.896
Sorry I'm late. It's fine.

94
00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.696
I'm sure I don't need to tell you

95
00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.840
the effect of the Yeabsley leak is...

96
00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:23.760
devastating.

97
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.496
Most of our tools have been
rendered nugatory

98
00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:30.936
and will have to be built again
from scratch.

99
00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.640
Our priority now is to keep
what little we do have left secure.

100
00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.856
As of 2000 hours today. Eastern Time.

101
00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:43.896
the NSA's intelligence-sharing
arrangement with the UK

102
00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.080
is withdrawn. for the foreseeable future.

103
00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:50.696
Er. Mark...

104
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:54.136
signals cooperation between
our two countries...

105
00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.176
goes back 75 years and it plays a vital...

106
00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.120
This decision comes from the
Commander-in-chief personally...

107
00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.000
and is not open for discussion.

108
00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.296
The question we're all asking
ourselves here is why the hell

109
00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.776
you re-employed
a loose cannon like John Yeabsley

110
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.280
in the first place.

111
00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.160
Hiya. Hi. You all right?

112
00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.296
Where do you want me. Sarge?

113
00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.896
Get yourself round the back.

114
00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.056
Make sure no press are trying
to get in through the garden.

115
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.176
Hey. You're gonna need a mask. Sandy.

116
00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.320
I'm just going straight through.
thank you.

117
00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.440
Hiya.

118
00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.680
Sorry. Thanks.

119
00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.120
James. it's me again.

120
00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.376
Please call me back.

121
00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.216
I know you're angry.

122
00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.760
We need to talk.

123
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.960
Come on.

124
00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.376
GCHQ intelligence analyst
John Yeabsley.

125
00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:09.216
seen yesterday on Russian TV
admitting responsibility

126
00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.016
for a massive leak of GCHQ secrets.

127
00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.856
could Not have been in Moscow
yesterday. Back to Dan.

128
00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.936
Yes!

129
00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.136
Yes. yes. yes. I knew it.

130
00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.616
I knew it... in light of what police
are saying here tonight.

131
00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.456
the interview shown yesterday
on Russian TV

132
00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:27.536
seems likely now. somehow.
to have been faked.

133
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.736
as he was clearly already dead.
here in Cheltenham.

134
00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.760
when he was supposedly being taped
in Moscow.

135
00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.976
Dear. A mountain of code.

136
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:02.256
Perhaps it will make you. er...
check your assumptions.

137
00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.160
Remember the Nigerian prince.

138
00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.616
If you find yourself scouring through

139
00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.176
thousands and thousands
of lines of code.

140
00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.816
that's probably...

141
00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.800
exactly what they're expecting you to do.

142
00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:24.176
Don't.

143
00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:28.360
Do something else. unexpected.

144
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:35.000
You have to think outside the box.

145
00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:44.040
If you can't. then you have to
find someone... who can.

146
00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.336
Should I offer to help?

147
00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.296
No. she doesn't need any help.

148
00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.200
She knows exactly where
everything is. Don't you. dear?

149
00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.936
It's the first time we've had one
of Gabe's work friends to visit.

150
00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.656
Isn't it. Gabe?

151
00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:14.896
We'd almost given up hope.

152
00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:16.016
Sorry?

153
00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.016
He was turned down by
so many employers before GCHQ.

154
00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.456
We moved here so we could look
after him.

155
00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.360
He can't live alone. obviously.

156
00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.776
I know you said you didn't want to
help me any more but I'm in trouble.

157
00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.800
What kind of trouble?

158
00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.600
What I'm saying is...
I've got GCHQ into trouble.

159
00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:39.920
OK. what I mean is...

160
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.416
I didn't realise I was being used.

161
00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.576
I think there's
a third-stage malware. Gabriel.

162
00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.520
hidden inside the code. I need to find it.

163
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.576
Someone tried to warn me about it.
that it was really dangerous. but...

164
00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:56.056
it's only now
I think I know what he meant.

165
00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.896
Who warned you?
That's not important now.

166
00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:01.216
There's been a massive leak of data
from GCHQ. right?

167
00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.216
Incredibly damaging.

168
00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.736
I think that's what the third stage does.

169
00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.376
I think there's some hidden part
of the original malware

170
00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.720
that was built to steal our data.

171
00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.656
But I can't find it.

172
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.680
I've been back through the code
line by line. There's nothing.

173
00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.216
That's the puzzle. Gabriel.

174
00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.376
I'm asking if you'd...

175
00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.520
It's OK. Saara. I get it.

176
00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.056
Where are you going. Gabe?

177
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.776
Sorry.

178
00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.320
But what about the curfew?

179
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.720
It's obfuscated. You don't need to... Wait.

180
00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.816
I was just trying to say you don't
need to waste time on it.

181
00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:58.456
The original code's obfuscated.

182
00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.896
They included all this garbage
so that anti-virus software

183
00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.456
wouldn't recognise it as malware.

184
00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.816
How many lines of garbage?

185
00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.456
I don't know. Thousands?

186
00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.896
We stripped them out
so we could work on it.

187
00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.496
Tea? But before you stripped them out.

188
00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:12.736
you tried to get it to run in a sandbox.

189
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.280
That's right. How did you know?

190
00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.096
What happened?

191
00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.136
Nothing. It didn't run.

192
00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.520
They designed it so that it...
I... think it did.

193
00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:28.056
It didn't. Gabriel.
I tried it again and again.

194
00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.656
It just sat there.

195
00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.320
I watched. Nothing happened.

196
00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:35.320
You need to learn to look at
the garbage in a different way.

197
00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.696
It's all about patterns.

198
00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.016
Finding the code
hidden within the garbage.

199
00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.776
But in this case.
it's more complicated than normal.

200
00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.296
Usually.
there'd be one character of code.

201
00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:48.856
And. say. five characters of garbage.

202
00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.976
In that case.
you just need to write a script

203
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.456
to read one character in six.

204
00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.296
So you're saying it's not all garbage?

205
00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.840
Then...

206
00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.056
there's where the number of real
code and garbage characters vary

207
00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.256
according to a regular pattern.
Say one in four. then one in three.

208
00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.176
then one in two. And back up again.

209
00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:09.200
And that's what we've got here
in the BT code? No.

210
00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.776
This is more complicated.

211
00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.416
Here. there's no simple pattern.

212
00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:19.496
The code characters
and garbage characters vary

213
00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:20.656
according to an algorithm.

214
00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.376
So. we can't extract the hidden code
unless we know the algorithm?

215
00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.080
I've worked out the algorithm.
That's what took me the time.

216
00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.256
There's your third stage.

217
00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.720
Hidden inside of what you thought
was just garbage.

218
00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.160
That's a data scraper.

219
00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.840
That's how it mined our files.

220
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.016
That must be the MAC address
of your sandbox.

221
00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.616
That's how it broke into our system.

222
00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:56.696
It can't be.

223
00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.896
Yes. I think so.

224
00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:59.976
But how could they possibly know that?

225
00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.896
A MAC address is like a fingerprint.

226
00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:03.456
How could someone in Russia

227
00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:07.376
know the address of a particular
computer at GCHQ? It's impossible.

228
00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.896
No. it's obvious. Obvious? How?

229
00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.600
Someone must have told them.

230
00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.336
OK. Even if that is true.

231
00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.616
it doesn't explain
how they got the data out.

232
00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.320
This malware doesn't communicate.

233
00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:37.320
It exfiltrates as email.

234
00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.136
The data goes out as attachments.

235
00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:45.696
The emails get lost in the flood of
all our other email traffic.

236
00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.160
No-one notices.

237
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.376
They've moved on from NSA exploits.
by the way.

238
00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.816
Now they're taking our own stuff.

239
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.336
What? The emails are still going out.

240
00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.920
What?!

241
00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.536
They must know what we're doing.

242
00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.576
Every time I cut a link to a domain.
they set up a new one.

243
00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.719
We're losing a massive amount
of data every second.

244
00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:57.696
The scraper you found in the garbage -

245
00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:01.256
can you shut it down.
stop all this at source?

246
00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:03.616
Of course. Then do it.

247
00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.720
Please.

248
00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.296
Is that it? Yes.

249
00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:35.336
You've stopped it?

250
00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.416
Of course.
Why do you sound so surprised?

251
00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.600
You're brilliant.

252
00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.440
I owe you an apology.

253
00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.720
You're right. You do.

254
00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:46.600
I'm sorry.

255
00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:50.400
What you did last night was amazing.

256
00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.776
As well as in Bradford.

257
00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:00.136
the central Mosque in Southall
was fire-bombed

258
00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.576
while a service was taking place.

259
00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:05.056
A spokesperson for
the Muslim Council of Britain

260
00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:09.376
blamed the attack. one of dozens
reported in the last 36 hours.

261
00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:11.016
on the breakdown in public order

262
00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:13.120
in the aftermath of the disputed election.

263
00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:18.600
What is it?

264
00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:21.920
They're attacking mosques again.

265
00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:25.000
My brother works at a mosque
in Swindon.

266
00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:30.640
Well. you should go.

267
00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:42.336
We read about it every day in the papers

268
00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.336
and on our phones.

269
00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:46.696
we hear about it on the radio.

270
00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:50.176
we speak about it every morning
with our neighbours.

271
00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:52.320
we watch it every night on the TV news.

272
00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:58.296
And. of course. when they're
attacking us in the streets.

273
00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:00.200
when they're burning our mosques...

274
00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:03.040
we want to strike back.

275
00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:06.096
Why wouldn't we?

276
00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:07.680
It's only human.

277
00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:12.400
It sounds easy. brothers and sisters...

278
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:15.400
as do all the words of Shaytan.

279
00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:19.616
He speaks to us when we're angry.

280
00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:23.736
He fans the flames
of our completely reasonable anger.

281
00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:25.680
which comes from fear...

282
00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:30.560
and the desire to protect those we love.

283
00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:37.776
But we don't protect them.
brothers and sisters.

284
00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:41.496
by meeting violence with violence.

285
00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:44.856
Violence only breeds more violence.
more hatred.

286
00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:49.560
We hit back and they hit us again.
even harder.

287
00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:55.136
The way of Allah. Subhanahu wa-ta'ala.

288
00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:59.320
is the harder way.
the more courageous way.

289
00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.056
The voice of Shaytan rages in our ears.

290
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.120
blasting out all other sound.

291
00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:11.520
You will hear the voice of Allah.
Subhanahu wa-ta'ala...

292
00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.960
when you are quiet...

293
00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:18.600
when you are at rest...

294
00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:22.760
when you are at peace.

295
00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:32.720
Saj?

296
00:24:59.680 --> 00:25:00.880
Hey. what's up?

297
00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:03.760
Shut the door. Yeah.

298
00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:09.056
What is it?

299
00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:12.056
I've just been speaking to
the Prime Minister.

300
00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:16.416
Apparently. MI5's found some
compromising material

301
00:25:16.440 --> 00:25:18.519
on the Foreign Secretary's laptop.

302
00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:23.736
What kind of material?

303
00:25:23.760 --> 00:25:26.560
I'm not sure.
They're sending it over. the laptop.

304
00:25:28.280 --> 00:25:29.736
Inappropriate communications

305
00:25:29.760 --> 00:25:31.856
with someone inside
the Russian government -

306
00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:33.456
that's all I've been told.

307
00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:36.040
Highly prejudicial to national security.

308
00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:38.920
For fuck's sake.

309
00:25:39.920 --> 00:25:42.736
Surely even they must know
that's a Russian plant?

310
00:25:42.760 --> 00:25:45.216
I don't know.
It looks authentic. apparently.

311
00:25:45.240 --> 00:25:48.736
None of the usual signs of
crashing around inside a computer.

312
00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:52.440
If it's a plant. it's a clever one.
hard to prove.

313
00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:56.680
Anyway. she's had to resign.

314
00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:03.880
We're being played. aren't we?

315
00:26:05.600 --> 00:26:08.576
Have been. At every stage.

316
00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:10.800
Yeah. Yeah.

317
00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:15.056
And very convenient that we should
lose our best friend in government

318
00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:16.400
at this precise moment.

319
00:26:20.840 --> 00:26:22.840
Secretary of State for Defence.

320
00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:29.616
I said after the BT attack that.

321
00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:31.496
if we didn't respond robustly.

322
00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:34.296
we'd be hit again and we have been.

323
00:26:34.320 --> 00:26:38.600
Our election has been undermined and
our most sensitive secrets stolen.

324
00:26:40.040 --> 00:26:43.576
By any measure. this constitutes
the cyber equivalent

325
00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:46.000
of an armed attack on
the United Kingdom.

326
00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:49.400
An act of war.

327
00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:55.080
Head of operations. GCHQ.

328
00:26:58.800 --> 00:27:04.256
I'm not disagreeing
that a strong response is required

329
00:27:04.280 --> 00:27:06.776
but you should be aware that
if you decide upon

330
00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:11.320
a symmetric cyberattack.
it will be highly escalatory.

331
00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:16.256
Truth is. they've been one step
ahead of us. provoking us.

332
00:27:16.280 --> 00:27:18.496
anticipating how we'll react
at every stage.

333
00:27:18.520 --> 00:27:22.160
It's vital that we do not react
as expected now.

334
00:27:23.120 --> 00:27:25.816
We should be careful of empty gestures

335
00:27:25.840 --> 00:27:28.000
that have profound consequences.

336
00:27:29.280 --> 00:27:31.176
Empty gestures?

337
00:27:31.200 --> 00:27:35.240
Yes. Especially if there are other
motives for doing it.

338
00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:38.640
What other motives?

339
00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:42.056
Can I speak frankly?

340
00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:44.040
Of course.

341
00:27:46.480 --> 00:27:48.136
To shore up the position of a government

342
00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:50.416
whose legitimacy has been questioned.

343
00:27:50.440 --> 00:27:52.240
To distract attention.

344
00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:56.376
Is that what you think is going on here?

345
00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:59.616
With the greatest respect
to our colleague from GCHQ.

346
00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:00.976
Prime Minister.

347
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:03.760
that is a completely
outrageous suggestion.

348
00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:08.216
This country has either faced
an attack amounting to

349
00:28:08.240 --> 00:28:10.696
an act of war or it hasn't.

350
00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:13.096
And if it has. it is our duty

351
00:28:13.120 --> 00:28:16.296
as the properly constituted
government to respond.

352
00:28:16.320 --> 00:28:18.416
It's nothing to do with legitimacy

353
00:28:18.440 --> 00:28:20.560
or any other political considerations.

354
00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:28.616
Can I just remind us that
the then Attorney General

355
00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:33.016
made our red lines absolutely clear
in his 2018 speech?

356
00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:35.776
Use of cyber to manipulate the
electoral system

357
00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:37.296
explicitly constitutes

358
00:28:37.320 --> 00:28:39.896
an intervention in our domestic affairs.

359
00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:41.976
If. after that speech. we do nothing.

360
00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.496
we are basically saying it's OK

361
00:28:43.520 --> 00:28:45.336
to just roll your tanks into London.

362
00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:47.216
Yes. I see your point.

363
00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:49.936
Of course. if we retaliate.

364
00:28:49.960 --> 00:28:51.256
we might expose some of

365
00:28:51.280 --> 00:28:53.136
the things we ourselves are doing.

366
00:28:53.160 --> 00:28:57.176
within Russia's critical
national infrastructure.

367
00:28:57.200 --> 00:28:58.976
Which would leave us open to

368
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:01.776
the accusation of double standards.

369
00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:05.096
But if that is the way you wish
to go. Prime Minister.

370
00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:07.976
Danny can lay out some further options.

371
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:10.576
We don't need your options.

372
00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:12.639
The Army will be taking
the lead this time.

373
00:29:14.080 --> 00:29:16.136
Good luck with that.

374
00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:17.656
What was that?

375
00:29:17.680 --> 00:29:18.816
Nothing.

376
00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:24.016
Good. Because Russia has effectively
declared war on this country.

377
00:29:24.040 --> 00:29:25.856
And we. those of us around this table.

378
00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:28.816
are charged with
the defence of this nation.

379
00:29:28.840 --> 00:29:31.080
I require your support to do so.

380
00:29:46.280 --> 00:29:47.400
David.

381
00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:53.656
I'm sending you a team
from the National Cyber Force.

382
00:29:53.680 --> 00:29:57.176
I want you to build them an attack.
targeting the Russian arms industry.

383
00:29:57.200 --> 00:29:59.136
And I want it done today.

384
00:29:59.160 --> 00:30:01.800
Can you do that?
Put them out of action?

385
00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:06.536
We can certainly try.

386
00:30:06.560 --> 00:30:10.336
It's time to show us what we've
been paying for at GCHQ.

387
00:30:10.360 --> 00:30:13.560
All this money we've spent. It's
time to show us what you can do.

388
00:30:23.560 --> 00:30:25.760
I'm sorry. Saj.

389
00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:28.360
You were right.

390
00:30:30.840 --> 00:30:34.000
I should've thought more carefully
before I took the job at GCHQ.

391
00:30:35.520 --> 00:30:38.296
About the consequences for our family.

392
00:30:38.320 --> 00:30:40.216
I over-reacted.

393
00:30:40.240 --> 00:30:42.320
No. You didn't.

394
00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:45.440
You were right.

395
00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:48.680
I shouldn't have gone there.

396
00:30:54.360 --> 00:30:55.720
I've made a mistake.

397
00:30:56.920 --> 00:30:58.800
At work. What mistake?

398
00:31:01.080 --> 00:31:02.760
I suppose you can't say?

399
00:31:09.920 --> 00:31:11.960
I did something... that...

400
00:31:13.200 --> 00:31:15.496
I thought was really clever.

401
00:31:15.520 --> 00:31:17.256
It wasn't.

402
00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:20.440
It was incredibly stupid and gullible.

403
00:31:22.320 --> 00:31:24.680
And it's allowed something terrible
to happen.

404
00:31:25.920 --> 00:31:27.896
Are you sure?

405
00:31:27.920 --> 00:31:30.280
Because you always think
everything's your fault.

406
00:31:32.400 --> 00:31:33.760
You have no idea.

407
00:31:43.760 --> 00:31:45.816
Anyway. Dad was my fault.

408
00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:48.080
What? How is that your fault?

409
00:31:49.680 --> 00:31:51.496
He killed himself.

410
00:31:51.520 --> 00:31:54.016
He killed himself because I went
away to uni and left him.

411
00:31:54.040 --> 00:31:56.336
No. Saar... He did. I abandoned him.

412
00:31:56.360 --> 00:31:58.936
No. that's not what happened.
Saar... Yeah. he killed himself.

413
00:31:58.960 --> 00:32:00.600
He didn't kill himself.

414
00:32:02.320 --> 00:32:04.936
I mean. sorry to ruin this
"I'm to blame for everything"

415
00:32:04.960 --> 00:32:07.296
thing you've got going. but no...

416
00:32:07.320 --> 00:32:08.536
he didn't kill himself.

417
00:32:08.560 --> 00:32:12.856
I mean. if you'd... come home
you'd know that.

418
00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:16.416
It was an accident.
A signalman made a mistake.

419
00:32:16.440 --> 00:32:19.840
He sent a goods train up a line that
was supposed to be out of service.

420
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:22.816
Dad took a short cut across the track

421
00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:24.776
and the train hit him.

422
00:32:24.800 --> 00:32:26.960
It wasn't suicide.

423
00:32:30.280 --> 00:32:33.416
You're just saying that
because suicide is haram. No.

424
00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:36.800
I swear on Mum's life -
that's what happened.

425
00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:41.656
You may have behaved like a shit
not coming to see him

426
00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:43.680
but he didn't commit suicide.

427
00:32:57.880 --> 00:32:59.120
I liked your sermon.

428
00:33:00.600 --> 00:33:02.200
Thanks.

429
00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:05.560
I mean. I...

430
00:33:06.720 --> 00:33:09.120
I agreed with...
I agreed with everything you said.

431
00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:23.280
Do you think I should resign?

432
00:33:26.200 --> 00:33:27.920
That's up to you. but...

433
00:33:29.280 --> 00:33:32.776
we'd be losing the last real voice
of moderation around the table.

434
00:33:32.800 --> 00:33:36.336
There'd be nobody left
to protect the staff.

435
00:33:36.360 --> 00:33:39.160
Well. what about you? Me?!

436
00:33:40.760 --> 00:33:43.999
They'd sack me 15 seconds after
you're out the door.

437
00:33:46.840 --> 00:33:49.240
Sorry. They're ready.

438
00:33:51.040 --> 00:33:52.080
"They're ready."

439
00:33:57.640 --> 00:34:01.896
I told Barbara to take the kids.

440
00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:04.656
go and stay with her parents in France.

441
00:34:04.680 --> 00:34:06.640
You're joking. No. absolutely not.

442
00:34:08.240 --> 00:34:10.576
It's not that bad. is it?

443
00:34:10.600 --> 00:34:13.976
I don't know. But I'm pretty sure
this - us attacking them -

444
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:16.456
it's exactly what they want us to do.

445
00:34:16.480 --> 00:34:18.000
You have to ask yourself why.

446
00:34:19.560 --> 00:34:21.720
Do you think I should get Freddie out?

447
00:34:24.880 --> 00:34:25.880
Maybe.

448
00:34:47.560 --> 00:34:49.056
Ready. boss.

449
00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:51.216
OK. what happens now?

450
00:34:51.240 --> 00:34:53.736
You stand aside
and we press the button.

451
00:34:53.760 --> 00:34:55.456
That way it's covered by the rules of war

452
00:34:55.480 --> 00:34:56.840
and you don't end up in The Hague.

453
00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:02.760
OK. Finn. Up you get.

454
00:35:18.320 --> 00:35:20.599
Control-E.

455
00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:32.400
How long will it take to have an effect?

456
00:35:33.560 --> 00:35:34.840
No time at all.

457
00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:37.680
It's happening now.

458
00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:06.696
Is this real?

459
00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:08.336
Real?

460
00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:10.280
I doubt it.

461
00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:44.536
Danny. can I have a word with you?

462
00:36:44.560 --> 00:36:45.936
What is it?

463
00:36:45.960 --> 00:36:47.160
Private word.

464
00:36:55.960 --> 00:36:58.296
What is it? Our comms are down.

465
00:36:58.320 --> 00:37:00.216
Sorry? All our comms are down.

466
00:37:00.240 --> 00:37:01.736
I wanted to speak to you out here

467
00:37:01.760 --> 00:37:04.136
because I didn't want to create a panic.

468
00:37:04.160 --> 00:37:05.536
What. just Army comms?

469
00:37:05.560 --> 00:37:07.056
To be honest. we're not sure.

470
00:37:07.080 --> 00:37:10.096
I managed to get through to the MOD
on one of your landlines.

471
00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:13.336
They're requesting
that GCHQ help re-establish contact.

472
00:37:13.360 --> 00:37:15.640
With...? With UK Armed Forces.

473
00:37:17.320 --> 00:37:19.856
Sorry. Danny. The Defence Secretary
is on the line.

474
00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:20.936
Which channel?

475
00:37:20.960 --> 00:37:23.960
No. I mean he's actually
on the line. He's on the phone.

476
00:37:29.560 --> 00:37:31.056
Richard. We've just heard.

477
00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:32.096
Heard what?

478
00:37:32.120 --> 00:37:33.816
About your loss of comms.

479
00:37:33.840 --> 00:37:35.296
Not that.

480
00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:39.536
The nuclear submarine control system
is unresponsive.

481
00:37:39.560 --> 00:37:41.096
It may have been hacked.

482
00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:42.616
What?

483
00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:44.800
Are you... Are you absolutely sure?

484
00:37:45.920 --> 00:37:46.960
Richard?

485
00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:49.240
Richard?

486
00:37:52.640 --> 00:37:54.856
If there's anything
still working around here.

487
00:37:54.880 --> 00:37:59.000
try and get me NSA up on
the satellite. er. on this one. OK.

488
00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:24.439
I've decided to leave...

489
00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:27.040
OK.

490
00:38:31.040 --> 00:38:32.656
But if you've made a mess.

491
00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:35.416
don't leave before you've cleared it up.

492
00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:38.000
You should never leave someone else
to clear up your mess. Saar.

493
00:38:48.640 --> 00:38:49.920
Mitch.

494
00:38:51.160 --> 00:38:52.376
Danny.

495
00:38:52.400 --> 00:38:54.776
Look. I know you guys aren't talking
to us at the moment

496
00:38:54.800 --> 00:38:55.976
but I thought you should know

497
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:59.296
somebody just hacked our
nuclear submarine control system.

498
00:38:59.320 --> 00:39:00.576
What? You're kidding?

499
00:39:00.600 --> 00:39:03.096
Plus... all of our military comms
are down.

500
00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:05.056
The Russians have just spent
the last two hours

501
00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:07.176
exaggerating the effect of
a very targeted attack

502
00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:08.416
on a couple or arms factories

503
00:39:08.440 --> 00:39:11.656
to make whatever it is they're doing
look like self-defence.

504
00:39:11.680 --> 00:39:14.456
And my guess is. they've been
planning this for a long time.

505
00:39:14.480 --> 00:39:16.496
Yeah. the problem is
we're seeing those images

506
00:39:16.520 --> 00:39:18.976
of hospital fires too. Danny...
Yeah. they're fakes. Mitch.

507
00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:20.960
Well. they look pretty real to us.

508
00:39:22.560 --> 00:39:24.896
I've gotta tell you.
there's not a lot of warm feelings

509
00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:26.520
towards you guys here at the moment.

510
00:39:29.440 --> 00:39:32.560
We could really do with
some help right now. Mitch.

511
00:39:35.040 --> 00:39:37.936
Next. please. Come on through.

512
00:39:37.960 --> 00:39:39.599
Arms up. please.

513
00:39:41.320 --> 00:39:42.760
You can't use that in here.

514
00:39:49.160 --> 00:39:51.736
You can't use that here. Turn it off. now.

515
00:39:51.760 --> 00:39:55.296
OK. But I've got to write this down.

516
00:39:55.320 --> 00:39:57.080
Have you got any paper?

517
00:41:29.840 --> 00:41:31.616
Saara. wait.

518
00:41:31.640 --> 00:41:33.536
I've got nothing to say to you.

519
00:41:33.560 --> 00:41:36.216
Please.
I think you're about to be attacked.

520
00:41:36.240 --> 00:41:38.976
The UK. I've got something
to give you that will stop it.

521
00:41:39.000 --> 00:41:41.056
I don't believe you. Vadim.

522
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:43.576
It's just another provocation.

523
00:41:43.600 --> 00:41:45.856
Anyway. I thought you said
in Harrogate they'd kill you.

524
00:41:45.880 --> 00:41:48.576
I don't care any more.
I don't care what happens to me.

525
00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:50.120
This is too important.

526
00:41:51.480 --> 00:41:52.760
Look at this.

527
00:42:06.600 --> 00:42:07.976
What is that?

528
00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:10.600
It's you. At your desk in GCHQ.

529
00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:30.816
OK. You hacked the CCTV.

530
00:42:30.840 --> 00:42:32.896
So what? What does that prove?

531
00:42:32.920 --> 00:42:35.816
Saara. please. There isn't much time.

532
00:42:35.840 --> 00:42:37.856
You have to trust me.

533
00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:39.840
You have to think outside the box.

534
00:42:41.280 --> 00:42:42.936
What?

535
00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:44.280
What did you say?

536
00:42:51.280 --> 00:42:54.416
JSSO's showing unidentified aircraft
entering our airspace

537
00:42:54.440 --> 00:42:56.296
and none of the other systems are
showing it.

538
00:42:56.320 --> 00:42:58.136
The RAF don't seem
to have been scrambled yet.

539
00:42:58.160 --> 00:43:00.376
But it is possible we are under attack.

540
00:43:00.400 --> 00:43:02.496
But it's just another hack.
isn't it? Fake news?

541
00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:06.536
What if it's real this time.
you know. like crying wolf?

542
00:43:06.560 --> 00:43:08.656
How can we take that chance?

543
00:43:08.680 --> 00:43:10.816
What. an invasion? Why not?

544
00:43:10.840 --> 00:43:13.976
We've been underestimating Putin
for ten years.

545
00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:16.656
All the way through we've been
asking. what's the bigger picture?

546
00:43:16.680 --> 00:43:19.216
The one thing we've never considered
is that he might just

547
00:43:19.240 --> 00:43:21.736
be insane enough
to have territorial ambitions.

548
00:43:21.760 --> 00:43:24.256
What if this whole thing is about
separating us

549
00:43:24.280 --> 00:43:25.776
from Europe and the Americans

550
00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:28.600
so that when this moment came.
we'd be alone?

551
00:43:30.640 --> 00:43:31.856
Not now. Saara.

552
00:43:31.880 --> 00:43:35.400
Danny. you absolutely HAVE
to come and see this. Right now.

553
00:43:37.280 --> 00:43:40.296
It's the CCTV - so what?
Saara. I don't have time for this.

554
00:43:40.320 --> 00:43:43.376
You have to turn it off. Please.

555
00:43:43.400 --> 00:43:46.080
I can't show you what I've got
to show you until you turn it off.

556
00:43:49.080 --> 00:43:50.360
Shut down the CCTV.

557
00:43:51.440 --> 00:43:53.096
Really?

558
00:43:53.120 --> 00:43:54.520
Yeah. Do it.

559
00:43:59.080 --> 00:44:00.976
They hacked the system.

560
00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:02.976
The FSB were watching
everything we're doing.

561
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:05.656
They can't. It's air-gapped.

562
00:44:05.680 --> 00:44:07.096
How do you know?

563
00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:09.400
Cos I've just been inside their computer.

564
00:44:14.280 --> 00:44:17.376
I'm sending you something now.
Two things.

565
00:44:17.400 --> 00:44:19.536
You can use them
to trade with the Americans.

566
00:44:19.560 --> 00:44:20.896
to bring them back in.

567
00:44:20.920 --> 00:44:23.760
As soon as that happens.
Putin will back down.

568
00:44:28.120 --> 00:44:30.176
During this first phase.

569
00:44:30.200 --> 00:44:34.736
we are degrading the capability
and resolve of our enemy.

570
00:44:34.760 --> 00:44:37.776
as well as discrediting his institutions

571
00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:41.896
and leadership with espionage.
assassination.

572
00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:45.136
manipulation of social media.
cyberattacks.

573
00:44:45.160 --> 00:44:46.456
faking of imagery.

574
00:44:46.480 --> 00:44:49.296
all with the aim of
creating disillusionment.

575
00:44:49.320 --> 00:44:51.720
confusion and. and... And chaos.

576
00:44:52.920 --> 00:44:55.776
By the time war is openly declared.

577
00:44:55.800 --> 00:44:57.216
the enemy's ability... War?

578
00:44:57.240 --> 00:45:00.096
To defend himself will be
significantly reduced... Danny?

579
00:45:00.120 --> 00:45:02.016
We're receiving a data dump.

580
00:45:02.040 --> 00:45:03.376
Where from?

581
00:45:03.400 --> 00:45:04.400
Russia.

582
00:45:08.120 --> 00:45:09.160
OK. let's go.

583
00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:14.576
Strategic situation. His relationships

584
00:45:14.600 --> 00:45:18.400
with his allies are
fatally undermined. one by one.

585
00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:24.880
It's mostly code. There's terabytes of it.

586
00:45:27.040 --> 00:45:30.480
I think it's the FSB's
offensive cyber exploits.

587
00:45:34.040 --> 00:45:35.200
My God!

588
00:45:36.360 --> 00:45:38.000
This puts us back in the game.

589
00:45:45.680 --> 00:45:48.536
So. how... How this all is to be achieved?

590
00:45:48.560 --> 00:45:53.896
How do you ensure that.
the final phase. the war is won?

591
00:45:53.920 --> 00:45:57.216
The war is won using a technique

592
00:45:57.240 --> 00:46:00.096
called reflexive control.

593
00:46:00.120 --> 00:46:03.056
This is the predetermining

594
00:46:03.080 --> 00:46:06.216
the enemy's behaviour
in Russia's favour.

595
00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:09.800
We define our ultimate objective.

596
00:46:14.560 --> 00:46:16.376
We define our ultimate objective -

597
00:46:16.400 --> 00:46:18.400
the total defeat of our enemy.

598
00:46:46.600 --> 00:46:49.720
